<DocsLayout title="Introduction" hidePrevNext>
  <h1>Identity</h1>
  <p>
    Authentication and user-management as a single, deployable container.
    Pull a pinned image, point it at a datastore (Postgres for production,
    or embedded SQLite for a single node),
    and you have email/password signup, passkeys, TOTP, OAuth, JWT issuance,
    sessions, and an admin user-management surface — all over Connect-RPC
    on HTTP/JSON.
  </p>

  <h2>What you get</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Email + password</strong> — signup, login, change, recovery-email reset, lockout</li>
    <li><strong>Passkeys (WebAuthn)</strong> — registration and login flows</li>
    <li><strong>TOTP (2FA)</strong> — setup, verify, recovery codes</li>
    <li><strong>OAuth login</strong> — Google, Microsoft, GitHub, Apple (server-owned authorization-code exchange)</li>
    <li><strong>QR cross-device login</strong> — initiate on a new device, approve from a logged-in one</li>
    <li><strong>JWT issuance</strong> with key rotation, plus <code>/.well-known/jwks.json</code> for downstream services</li>
    <li><strong>Sessions</strong> — list, revoke, sign-out-everywhere</li>
    <li><strong>Admin user management</strong> — invite, deactivate, reactivate, reset password, set quota</li>
    <li><strong>Groups</strong> + membership</li>
    <li><strong>Audit log</strong> of all auth events</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How it deploys</h2>
  <p>
    One container, one image, one datastore. Deploy it once per product —
    each Project is a fully isolated user pool. The container
    listens on <code>:80</code> for Connect-RPC, <code>:9090</code> for
    Prometheus metrics.
  </p>

  <Code code={`docker run -p 80:80 -p 9090:9090 \\
  -e GATEWAY_REPO_DRIVER=postgres \\
  -e GATEWAY_POSTGRES_DSN=postgres://identity:secret@postgres:5432/identity \\
  -e GATEWAY_DEFAULT_PROJECT_ID=proj_my_product \\
  -e GATEWAY_PASSKEY_RP_ID=my-product.com \\
  -e GATEWAY_PASSKEY_ORIGIN=https://my-product.com \\
  -e GATEWAY_TOTP_ISSUER="My Product" \\
  ghcr.io/elloloop/identity:1.2.0`} lang="bash" title="docker run" />

  <h2>Storage layout</h2>
  <p>
    All persistent state lives in the datastore (Postgres or SQLite) as
    plain relational tables. Every row is scoped by <code>project_id</code>,
    which is the isolation boundary — multiple Projects can share one
    Postgres instance without seeing each other's data.
  </p>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Table</th><th>Holds</th></tr>
    <tr><td>users</td><td>Identities, one per <code>(project_id, email)</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>groups</td><td>Groups and memberships</td></tr>
    <tr><td>refresh_tokens</td><td>Sessions (hashed refresh tokens)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>passkeys</td><td>WebAuthn credentials</td></tr>
    <tr><td>totp_secrets</td><td>Encrypted TOTP secrets</td></tr>
    <tr><td>audit_events</td><td>Append-only audit log</td></tr>
  </table>

